    "opening": "Landscaping crew utilization is the share of available worker-hours used for the productive work your service model defines. To calculate it, divide productive worker-hours by available worker-hours for the same crew and period. Decide first whether productive time includes travel and setup: changing that definition changes the result. This guide uses illustrative USD costs and a simple weekly schedule to show whether a sold workload can actually fit.",
