    "title": "Corporate Headshot Pricing: Setup, People and Delivery",
    "seoTitle": "Corporate Headshot Pricing",
    "description": "Calculate corporate headshot pricing from setup, employee count and editing time. Compare booking sizes, minimum fees and photographer delivery capacity.",
    "metaDescription": "Calculate corporate headshot pricing from setup, employee count and editing time. Compare booking sizes, minimum fees and photographer delivery capacity.",
    "image": "/images/blog/corporate-headshot-pricing-editorial.webp",
    "alt": "Photographer making an employee portrait in an office with a portable backdrop and softbox.",
    "imageCaption": "AI-generated editorial illustration of an on-site employee portrait session.",
    "published": "2026-10-03",
    "modified": "2026-10-03",
    "opening": "Corporate headshot pricing works best when you separate the cost of bringing the studio to a business from the cost of photographing and delivering each person's portrait. Estimate the whole assignment, including scheduling, setup, selection and retouching, before quoting a per-person number. A twenty-person booking can spread setup costs efficiently; a five-person booking often cannot use the same rate. All USD figures below are fictional planning assumptions, not current US market averages.",
    "unit": "sessions",
